{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Obsolete: premise void. This ticket assumed the reconciler's --filter-local-ids engine plumbing became DEAD once 82bb removed the legacy reconcile route. It did not. 82bb landed via CL 2626 (remove legacy reconcile CLI) + CL 2641 (Restore engine filter-local-ids): the top-level 'rebar reconcile' CLI and '--mode reconcile-check' were removed, but --filter-local-ids was RETAINED on the engine entrypoint (python -m rebar_reconciler) because the live Jira DC harness (tests/external/live_jira_dc), which runs in GitHub Actions against a live Jira DC instance, is an ACTIVE consumer of it for mandatory inbound-create scoping (--only/--except is not equivalent for a not-yet-bound inbound Jira key). There is therefore no dead plumbing to remove. Closing as obsolete."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788566044736137001,"uuid":"c8c8c41c-b502-4e8e-bf6f-978c5167e0d3"}